      origins: "Ã‰cartÃ© evolved from the older game 'Triomphe' and emerged in its modern form during the Napoleonic era. It was the premier gambling and social game for the European aristocracy throughout the 1800s.",
      originCountries: [
        'France',
      ],
      timeline: [
        '1820s: Rules are standardized and publish in French gaming manuals.',
        '1840s: Reaches peak popularity in London and Paris clubs.',
