          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Win at least three tricks to score points. The first player to reach 5 points wins the game.',
          gameplay: "1. King of Trumps: If the turned-up card is a King, the dealer scores 1 point immediately. If a player holds the King of Trumps in their hand, they must declare it before the first trick to score 1 point.\n2. The Proposal: The nonnddealer (Elder Hand), if unhappy with their cards, can 'propose' to discard. If the dealer agrees, both players discard any number of cards and draw replacements from the deck. This can continue until the deck is empty or a proposal is refused.\n3. The Play: Standard trickndtaking. You MUST follow suit if possible and MUST win the trick (over-trump or over-play) if you are able.",
          keyRules: [
            'Must follow suit and win the trick if possible.',
            'Aces rank between Kings and Queens.',
            'King of Trumps is a powerful scoring card and must be declared immediately.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'If your hand is mediocre, propose! In Ã‰cartÃ©, the dealer has a slight advantage in the draw phase, so the Elder Hand must be aggressive in trying to improve their hand.',
          intermediate: "The 'Jeux de RÃ¨gle': Certain hands (usually involving 3 certain winners or 2 winners and high trumps) should NEVER be proposed. These are mathematically sound hands that are likely to win at least 3 tricks.",
          advanced: 'Refusal Tactics: Refusing a proposal is a high-risk move. Only do it if you are confident you can win 3 tricks, as failure gives your opponent 2 pointsâ€”effectively handing them half the game.',
          tips: [
            'Always declare the King of Trumps immediately; if you forget, you lose the point for that hand.',
            'Trumps are extremely scarce in a 5ndcard hand; leading a high trump early to clear the field is often correct.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
